8 1111 #uuid "ff259840-0fb8-5d40-bfdf-e0a21b1dc174" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334609 1034 "2" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535161 true] [17592186334609 1111 #uuid "272fe965-ca5a-5092-b534-d27f749f26a8" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334610 1034 "6" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535161 true] [17592186334610 1111 #uuid "2a0255bb-fc8d-5c44-9bb5-9c90d39b6453" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334611 1034 "\\sqrt{8}" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535161 true] [17592186334611 1111 #uuid "42f8451e-7a70-59e3-8741-a6ec21148a7d" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334612 1034 "\\sqrt{12}" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535161 true] [17592186334612 1111 #uuid "4fccd52c-fa00-5dd2-9b1b-f34b259ed99c" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334613 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334614 13194139535161 true] [17592186334613 1089 "q-42739" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334613 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535161 true] [17592186334613 1100 "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=t-1.$" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334613 1113 #uuid "2a226526-c78d-5b45-912b-bc1bae613541" 13194139535161 true] [17592186334613 1145 "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(t-1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its nor